(575,"Why 1 percent of users can drive 75 percent of AI costs","Pricing specialist Ulrik Lehrskov-Schmidt explains on SaaStr the double hockey stick pattern in AI products, where a small share of heavy users drives most costs and gross margins fall from 85 to 90 percent to 55 percent, with lessons from Figma, Clay and Higgsfield."),
